## Step 5: Tier 2 controller test coverage for EventsController, HomeController, MyEventsController

### Status
Implemented.

### GitHub Issue
#59

### Summary
Cover the existing controller surface — `EventsController` and its partials, `HomeController`,
`MyEventsController` — using the harness from Step 4.

### Motivation
Controllers hold nearly all business logic in this app, so this is the highest-leverage
coverage in the initiative.

### Proposed Changes
- **Controller test infrastructure** (`WhenWorksWeb.Tests/Fixtures/`): `ControllerTestContext`
  (real `DefaultHttpContext`/`ControllerContext` wiring — `ClaimsPrincipal`, request cookies,
  `RequestServices` from `AddControllersWithViews()` so `TryValidateModel`/`TempData` work, and a
  minimal `StubUrlHelper` for `Url.RouteUrl`/`Url.Action` since real route resolution needs a full
  endpoint pipeline); `TestUserManagerFactory` (a real `UserManager<ApplicationUser>` resolved
  from a small DI container using `AddIdentityCore().AddEntityFrameworkStores<ApplicationDbContext>()`
  — not `new UserStore<ApplicationUser>(db)` directly, which fails to compile because
  `ApplicationUser`'s `required` members can't satisfy `UserStore<TUser>`'s `new()` constraint);
  `EventsControllerTestFixture` (shared base wiring a real `EventsController` with a single
  `EphemeralDataProtectionProvider` instance reused across every `CreateController()` call in a
  test, so a cookie protected during a simulated SignIn request can be unprotected by a later
  simulated Home request in the same test).
- `WhenWorksWeb.Tests/TestData/ApplicationUserBuilder.cs` — added for parity with the other entity
  builders, needed once controller tests required real signed-in users.
- `Controllers/HomeControllerTests.cs` — Index/Privacy/Error. (The spec originally described this
  file as covering "create/join-by-code entry points," but those actions are actually on
  `EventsController`, not `HomeController` — `HomeController` only serves Index/Privacy/Error.)
- `Controllers/EventsControllerTests.cs` (core: Create/Join),
  `Controllers/EventsControllerSignInTests.cs` (GET/POST SignIn — new participant creation,
  duplicate display name/color, missing/incorrect/correct rejoin code, conflicting account
  owner), `Controllers/EventsControllerHomeTests.cs` (Home action plus the shared access-cookie
  flow — including a full real sign-in-then-home round trip through actual cookie
  protect/unprotect, and a tampered-cookie case proving the cookie gets deleted rather than
  crashing the request) — mirroring the controller's own partial-class file split.
- `Controllers/MyEventsControllerTests.cs` — Index (challenge when unauthenticated, lists only
  created/joined events), Delete for both "event" (creator-only, Forbid otherwise) and
  "participant" modes, including a test that a participant's chat messages get their
  `ParticipantId` nulled rather than orphaned/rejected — the real FK-constraint behavior a SQLite
  backend (not EF Core InMemory) is what makes this test meaningful.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Every public action on the three controllers has at least one success-path and one
  failure-path test, where a failure path exists.
- `dotnet test` passes for all new controller tests (99 tests total as of this step).

### Out of Scope
- Authorization/anti-forgery-specific coverage (Step 7) — this step covers business-logic
  correctness, not security boundaries.
- Any Tier 3 full-pipeline test (Step 6).

### Dependencies
Step 4 (SQLite harness and entity builders).

