## Step 8: Stop hook to auto-run affected tests

### Status
Implemented.

### GitHub Issue
#62

### Summary
Add a Claude Code `settings.json` hook that automatically runs the relevant test class(es)
once per turn, for any `Controllers/`, `Services/`, or `Models/` source file that changed and
hasn't been tested since.

### Motivation
The enforcement rule documented in Step 2 relies on it actually being followed every time.
This closes the loop with an automated check that surfaces regressions immediately instead
of relying on memory alone.

### Design change from the original proposal
The spec originally called for a `PostToolUse` hook (firing after each Edit/Write call). That
was changed to a **`Stop` hook** (firing once when Claude finishes responding) after discussion
surfaced two problems with the original design:
- `PostToolUse` fires on *every* Edit/Write call, including repeated edits to the same file
  within one turn while iterating — noisy and wasteful.
- A time-window throttle (skip re-testing a file for N seconds after it was last tested) was
  considered and rejected: if a breaking edit happens and the file is never touched again, a
  throttle window could let that final, broken state go untested indefinitely.

The `Stop`-hook design instead fires once per turn and determines what to test from actual
content state, not tool-call timing or a timer: it diffs the current file content against a
hash recorded the last time each file was tested, so a file is tested exactly once after it
last changed, regardless of how many edits happened in between or how much later the next
`Stop` fires.

### Proposed Changes
- `.claude/hooks/run-affected-tests.ps1` — PowerShell script that: (1) lists files with
  uncommitted changes under `WhenWorksWeb/Controllers`, `WhenWorksWeb/Services`,
  `WhenWorksWeb/Models` via `git status`; (2) compares each against a SHA-256 hash recorded in
  `.claude/hooks/test-hook-state.json` (gitignored — runtime state, not shared config) from the
  last time it was tested, skipping anything unchanged; (3) maps remaining files to test
  class(es) by mirrored path/name, matching partial-class files (e.g. `EventsController.cs`,
  `.SignIn.cs`, `.Home.cs`, `.AccessCookie.cs`) by prefix against every
  `WhenWorksWeb.Tests/<Dir>/<BaseName>*Tests.cs`; (4) if nothing needs testing, exits silently;
  (5) otherwise runs one combined `dotnet test --filter <union>`, reports pass/fail via the
  Stop hook's `systemMessage` JSON output, and updates the state file's hashes for tested files
  regardless of outcome (a failure must surface once, not repeat on every later unrelated Stop).
- `.claude/settings.json` (new, checked in) — registers the hook on the `Stop` event.
- `.gitignore` — added `.claude/hooks/test-hook-state.json` (hook runtime state) and
  `.claude/settings.local.json` (previously only ignored via the developer's personal global
  git config, not portable to other checkouts of this repo).
- Verified directly (not just written and assumed correct): ran the script against a real
  changed `Services/` file (correct single-class match, correct test run, correct
  `systemMessage`), confirmed a second run against the same unchanged file produces no output,
  and confirmed a change to `EventsController.SignIn.cs` correctly matches and runs the union
  of all three `EventsController*Tests` classes (29 tests) via prefix matching.

### Acceptance Criteria
- A changed `Controllers/`/`Services/`/`Models/` file triggers exactly one `dotnet test` run
  (filtered to its corresponding test class(es)) the next time a turn ends, with results
  surfaced via `systemMessage`.
- An unchanged file (already tested at its current content) does not trigger another run.
- The hook never blocks or reverts anything, regardless of test outcome — always exits 0.

### Out of Scope
- A CI (GitHub Actions) gate — deferred to a future, separate decision (see epic #54).
- Coverage-gap detection (i.e. flagging when a change has *no* corresponding test at all) —
  this hook only re-runs existing tests, it doesn't verify new tests were added.

### Dependencies
Step 1 (test project must exist) and Step 2 (documented naming/path convention the hook's
mapping logic relies on). This is a Claude Code harness configuration change, not
application code.
